# Normalise every text file to LF, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# NB the working tree half is the part that matters. Git already stores LF, but on Windows
# core.autocrlf rewrites files to CRLF on checkout, and eslint-plugin-n's `n/hashbang` rule requires
# LF for any file carrying a shebang. So bin/rhtml.js -- untouched, correct in the repository -- fails
# `rhtml lint` on a Windows checkout, which since 9.0.0 also fails bin/prepush and blocks the push.
# `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf for this repo, so what a developer lints is what CI lints.
#
# NB `text=auto` still lets git detect binary content, so the png and jpg baselines below are belt and
# braces rather than a correction -- they are declared explicitly because silently line-ending-mangled
# images are expensive to notice.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
